WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.750
Your summer job: a
diner on a busy highway.

2
00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:06.880
It's Friday night, and
the orders are piling up.

3
00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.620
With one cook, the kitchen
turns out 10 meals an hour.

4
00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:13.280
Add a second cook, and it's 24.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:17.570
The manager is thrilled, and
plans to keep hiring all summer.

6
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.130
If a kitchen hires twice as many cooks,

7
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.900
why might it not make twice as many meals?

8
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.240
In this mission, you'll calculate total,

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.060
average and marginal
product for the kitchen.

10
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.730
Then you'll add cooks
one at a time and predict

11
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.900
what happens to total output.

12
00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.120
Your mission: figure out
why more workers do not

13
00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.770
always mean proportionally more output.
